-- title:
--   AT(P) contains the positivity patterns of the affine integer lattice spanned by P
-- statement:
--   Let $P \subseteq \{0,1\}^k$ and identify a Boolean tuple $x$ with the integer vector $\iota(x) \in \{0,1\}^k \subseteq \mathbb Z^k$. For odd $L$ let $\mathrm{AT}_L(x_1,\dots,x_L) = 1$ iff $\sum_{i=1}^{L} (-1)^{i-1} x_i > 0$, and let $\mathrm{AT}(P) = \bigcup_{L \text{ odd}} \mathrm{AT}_L(P)$, where $f(P)$ is the set of tuples obtained by applying $f$ column-wise to $L$ rows from $P$.
--
--   Let $\Lambda(P) \le \mathbb Z^k$ be the subgroup generated by all differences $\iota(v) - \iota(u)$ with $u, v \in P$. Then for every $x \in P$ and every $z \in \Lambda(P)$, the positivity pattern of $\iota(x) + z$, namely
--
--   $$
--   c \mapsto [\, \iota(x)_c + z_c > 0 \,],
--   $$
--
--   lies in $\mathrm{AT}(P)$.
--
--   So $\mathrm{AT}(P)$ contains the positivity patterns of the whole affine integer lattice $\iota(x) + \Lambda(P)$ spanned by $P$. The proof appends pairs of rows $(u, v)$ to an odd-length matrix, which adds $\iota(v) - \iota(u)$ to the vector of alternating column sums. The statement holds for arbitrary Boolean relations; the Hamming-weight case drives Claim 4.6 of Brakensiek–Guruswami, and the same lattice is the one behind affine (AIP-type) relaxations.
--
--   **Formalization Note** $\mathrm{AT}_L$ is `AT L` with 0-based indices (coordinate $i$ has sign $(-1)^{i}$), and $\mathrm{AT}(P)$ is `ATImage P`. The lattice is `AddSubgroup.closure` of the set of difference vectors in `Fin k → ℤ`.
-- source:
--   J. Brakensiek, V. Guruswami, Promise Constraint Satisfaction: Algebraic Structure and a Symmetric Boolean Dichotomy, arXiv:1704.01937v2, §4.2, proof of Claim 4.6, p. 17 (row-appending argument)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_PCSPBLPAff_Symmetric_Setting
import Definitions.Def_SymBoolPCSP_CFixing_Basic

open PCSPBLPAff.Symmetric
namespace SymBoolPCSP.CFixing

/-- The AT-image `AT(P) = ⋃_{L odd} AT_L(P)` contains the positivity pattern of every point `x + z`, where `x ∈ P` and `z` lies in the subgroup of `ℤ^k` generated by the differences `v - u` (`u, v ∈ P`). -/
theorem mem_ATImage_of_mem_diffClosure {k : ℕ} (P : Set (Fin k → Bool)) {x : Fin k → Bool}
    (hx : x ∈ P) {z : Fin k → ℤ}
    (hz : z ∈ AddSubgroup.closure {d : Fin k → ℤ | ∃ u ∈ P, ∃ v ∈ P,
        d = fun c => (if v c then 1 else 0) - (if u c then 1 else 0)}) :
    (fun c => decide (0 < (if x c then (1 : ℤ) else 0) + z c)) ∈ ATImage P := by sorry

end SymBoolPCSP.CFixing
